            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Sorry, this is more question to LazyVim than 'mini.files'. Example in 'mini.files' for `g~` mapping works with standalone 'mini.files' and with 'mini.clue' (as it is not enabled in 'mini.files' by default). The `g?` menu shows all buffer-local mappings, so the local `gc` might be added somewhere else (as it is not a part of 'mini.files').\r\n\r\nMy suggestion would be to ask in LazyVim or 'folke/which-key.nvim' discussions.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Sorry, this is more question to LazyVim than 'mini.files'. Example in 'mini.files' for <code class=\"notranslate\">g~</code> mapping works with standalone 'mini.files' and with 'mini.clue' (as it is not enabled in 'mini.files' by default). The <code class=\"notranslate\">g?</code> menu shows all buffer-local mappings, so the local <code class=\"notranslate\">gc</code> might be added somewhere else (as it is not a part of 'mini.files').</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">My suggestion would be to ask in LazyVim or 'folke/which-key.nvim' discussions.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Sorry, this is more question to LazyVim than 'mini.files'. Example in 'mini.files' for g~ mapping works with standalone 'mini.files' and with 'mini.clue' (as it is not enabled in 'mini.files' by default). The g? menu shows all buffer-local mappings, so the local gc might be added somewhere else (as it is not a part of 'mini.files').\nMy suggestion would be to ask in LazyVim or 'folke/which-key.nvim' discussions.",
